# The repo's .gitignore refuses every `.env.*`, which is right — `.env.prod` holds the signing key,
# the database password and the first owner's password, and `gen-secrets.sh` writes it here. But the
# EXAMPLE has to be in the repo or nobody knows what to fill in, so re-admit that one file by name.
!.env.prod.example

# Whatever backup.sh / restore.sh leave behind when they are run from this directory by hand.
*.dump
*.tar.gz
